      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F2_Madhuri_SSC_25.11.2022_D3.png\" style=\" width: 204px; height: 203px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Pythagoras theorem,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Sum of square of the other sides of the right-angled triangle is equal to the square of the hypotenuse.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n\n<p>According to question,</p>\n\n<p>DC = &radic;(13&sup2; - 12&sup2;) = &radic;(169 - 144) = &radic;25 = 5</p>\n\n<p>sin<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\phi\\)</span>&nbsp;= DC/BD = 5/13</p>\n\n<p>Let a line from D perpendicular to line AB at E,</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/03/F3_Madhuri_SSC_09.03.2023_D1.png\" style=\"height: 203px; width: 241px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>Then AE = AB - DC = 14 - 5 = 9</p>\n\n<p>tan&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\theta\\)</span>&nbsp;= DE/AE = BC/AE = 12/9 = 4/3</p>\n\n<p>Now,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{sin\\phi + tan\\theta}{sin\\phi - tan\\theta}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{\\frac{5}{13}+\\frac{4}{3}}{\\frac{5}{13}-\\frac{4}{3}}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>= - 67/37</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hence, The Required value is - 67/37.</strong></p>\n",
